# The webhook receiver's environment — copy to .env.receiver and fill in.
#
# Its own file, deliberately apart from .env: the receiver is the platform's one
# public process (TO-BE §5), and what it can leak is what it is handed. This
# file holds the App ids, the *refs* of their webhook secrets and the values
# those refs name — never a platform credential. compose hands it to the
# receiver alone; .env never reaches the receiver.
#
# The GitHub Apps whose webhooks point at the route, `<app id>=<secret ref>`,
# comma-separated; the ref is env:VAR / file:PATH / helper:NAME, never the value.
# The dev App's webhook alone covers every product repo it is installed on — do
# not add the reviewer/tester Apps: every App that delivers is one more wake, and
# so one more poll, per GitHub event.
WEBHOOK_APPS=123456=env:DEV_WEBHOOK_SECRET
DEV_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Where wakes go (a replica's WAKE_BIND) and where to listen. compose sets both;
# a bare `webhook-receiver serve` reads them here.
# WAKE_URL=http://control-plane:8081
# RECEIVER_BIND=0.0.0.0:8080
